<section class="ch" id="challenge"><div class="shell">
 <div class="ch-txt head"><p class="lab">The challenge</p><h2 class="claim">Thousands of government services, in one app, for millions of people.</h2>
 <p>TAMM is where citizens, residents, businesses and visitors in Abu Dhabi apply for government services, talk to customer service and track their requests. Before, each service lived with its own department. Bringing them into one app risked too much information, and journeys that broke between departments.</p></div>
</div></section><section class="ch" id="evaluation"><div class="shell">
 <div class="ch-txt head"><p class="lab">Heuristic evaluation</p><h2 class="claim">First, we reviewed the app as it was.</h2>
 <p>As a team, we went through the first version of the app screen by screen, against usability heuristics.</p></div>
 <div class="wide-m"><div class="he"><div class="he-opt he-a" data-he="a"><div class="he-stack"></div><div class="he-row2"><span class="he-lab"></span><div class="he-nav"><button type="button" data-d="-1" aria-label="Previous slide"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button><button type="button" data-d="1" aria-label="Next slide"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button></div></div></div></div></div>
</div></section><section class="ch" id="architecture"><div class="shell">
 <div class="ch-txt head"><p class="lab">Information architecture</p><h2 class="claim">From who owns a service, to what people need.</h2>
 <p>With what the evaluation showed, I led the rework of the app’s structure: from one built around government departments, to one built around people’s needs. Five places, each with a clear job. Home shows what needs attention. Services is where you find one. Support is where you get help and follow a case. Community is news and public holidays. Locker holds everything that is yours.</p></div>
 <div class="wide-m"><div class="st" style="--mt:17.6%" role="img" aria-label="The new information architecture, with the annotated list of changes behind it"><figure class="st-back"><img src="/work/tamm/i/5843d39eacf3.webp" alt=""></figure><figure class="st-front"><img src="/work/tamm/i/da8104456c7b.webp" alt=""></figure></div></div>
 <div class="ch-txt sub"><p class="lab">Testing the structure</p><h3>Then we went back to users.</h3>
 <p>We did not guess the new structure was better. Card sorting showed how people group the services, and a tree test checked whether they could find things in it: 8 tasks, 35 people.</p></div>
 <div class="tstats"><div class="o"><b>88%</b><span>success</span></div><div class="o"><b>75%</b><span>directness</span></div></div>
 <div class="wide-m"><div class="st" style="--mt:19.9%" role="img" aria-label="Tree test results for three tasks, with the card sort standardisation grid behind it"><figure class="st-back"><img src="/work/tamm/i/7a5d1bef2b45.webp" alt=""></figure><figure class="st-front"><img src="/work/tamm/i/14d40afa44fa.webp" alt=""></figure></div></div>
</div></section><section class="ch" id="design"><div class="shell">
 <div class="ch-txt head"><p class="lab">UI design</p><h2 class="claim">Then we designed it, section by section.</h2>
 <p>Three of us redesigned the whole app on the new structure. We split it into its sections and designed each one to the same rules, so it looks and works the same everywhere.</p></div>
 <div class="mods"><article class="mod"><div class="mod-t"><p class="lab">Onboarding</p><p>TAMM only offered login with UAE PASS. At the time UAE PASS was new: most residents did not know what it was, and did not have a verified account. So onboarding had to teach people how to become a verified UAE PASS user, and then log in. We prototyped different versions of that flow and tested them with residents in the real world, in sessions I moderated.</p></div><div class="mod-m"><div class="ob" role="img" aria-label="Onboarding: the login screen in front, then the upgrade popup, About UAE PASS and the kiosk finder, with two photos of the whiteboard from the field tests"><div class="ob-ph p1"><img src="/work/tamm/i/5927c62cfdc6.webp" alt=""></div><div class="ob-ph p2"><img src="/work/tamm/i/765127298524.webp" alt=""></div><div class="ob-ph p3"><img src="/work/tamm/i/c36713949388.webp" alt=""></div><div class="ob-ph p4"><img src="/work/tamm/i/28046a136b4a.webp" alt=""></div><figure class="ob-wb w1"><img src="/work/tamm/i/aa9adb8a58dd.webp" alt=""></figure><figure class="ob-wb w2"><img src="/work/tamm/i/b62b95ba3dcc.webp" alt=""></figure></div></div></article><article class="mod"><div class="mod-t"><p class="lab">Home</p><p>A home you can arrange to suit you.</p></div><div class="mod-m hx"><div class="hm" data-len="2722" data-stops="296,620,1016,1262,1706,2070,2456" role="img" aria-label="Home: the welcome popup that introduces the new home, the logged-in home scrolling through its widgets, and the widget editor"><div class="hm-ph l"><div class="hm-scr"><img class="full" src="/work/tamm/i/ca07e23fa466.webp" alt=""><div class="hm-sb"><span>9:41</span><i><svg viewBox="0 0 18 12"><rect x="0" y="8" width="3" height="4" rx="1"/><rect x="5" y="5.5" width="3" height="6.5" rx="1"/><rect x="10" y="3" width="3" height="9" rx="1"/><rect x="15" y="0" width="3" height="12" rx="1"/></svg><svg viewBox="0 0 16 12"><path d="M8 11.5 5.6 9a3.4 3.4 0 0 1 4.8 0zM3.5 6.9a6.4 6.4 0 0 1 9 0l-1.4 1.